    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măcĕtae</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măcĕdae</span></b> ),
			ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μακέται</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> (As a less usual form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μακεδόνες</span>,) <i>Macedonians</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Macetae locupletissimo imperio aucti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					9, 3, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Gen. plur.</i>
			Măcĕtūm. <i><span class="en">Stat. S.
				4, 6, 106</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 14, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2,
			647</span></i>; Claud. ap. <i><span class="en">Rufin. 2, 279</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. de Clar. Urb. 2,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Because Antiochus the Great was a descendant of Seleucus Nicator) =
			Syri, <i><span class="en">Sil. 13, 878</span></i>.</div>
